  <sys:String x:Key="Home.Title">Home</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.Subtitle">C# / WPF rewrite (a learning project). The goal is not to replace the existing software but to practise C# and industrial HMI engineering; the Delphi software stays in service and serves as the reference answer.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.MilestoneTitle">Milestones</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.M1">Skeleton runs: shell + DI/logging + contracts + test pipeline</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.M2">Channels + GR-3 protocol (golden cases included); verified on the real controller</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.M3">T0715 bending, end to end, with report output</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.M4">On-machine verification + second method (Marshall)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.StatusDone">Done</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.StatusTodo">Not started</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.CurrentMilestone">Current milestone</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.BoundaryTitle">M1 known boundaries</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Home.BoundaryText">M1-M3 have landed: GR-3 framing and the UDP channel (verified on the real controller), uplink parsing, the control engine and simulator, T0715 analysis and group statistics, the three-table schema and write layer, label-based reporting (zh/en factory templates), five UI pages, network-link monitoring with link-loss safeguards, and settings persistence (external config file Config\settings.json). Still open: on-machine check of the motor direction word and reset, and the second method (Marshall) in M4.</sys:String>

