  <sys:String x:Key="Exec.LinkAlarmTitle">Communication alarm</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Exec.LinkAlarmBodyRunning">Network link lost (**a test was running**): {0}&#10;{1}&#10;&#10;That run was aborted. A stop command was sent on a best-effort basis, but **the device state cannot be confirmed** — the link to the controller is UDP (connectionless): the frame may never have left this PC, and a "successful" send proves nothing.&#10;&#10;Check the machine and specimen on site NOW; after the link recovers the run will NOT resume automatically.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Exec.LinkUnknownAdapter">(adapter not identified)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Exec.Reconnected">Link restored — reconnected automatically (device config re-read)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Exec.ReconnectFailed">Automatic reconnect after link restore failed; click "Connect" to retry</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Exec.NoDeviceConfig">Not connected (device config A0 not read): live values are hidden (shown as --) because raw counts must not be mistaken for measurements. Click "Connect", or wait for automatic reconnect after the link recovers.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Exec.StopNotConfirmed">Motor stop NOT confirmed: no "motor stopped" status frame after the stop command — check the machine on site</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Exec.ForceCleaned">UI returned to idle: the previous run's cleanup was interrupted (the stop command got no ack). Check the machine state before continuing.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Exec.StopAlarmBody">Motor stop NOT confirmed: no "motor stopped" status frame arrived within 2 s after the stop command.&#10;&#10;The link is up, so this usually means the machine really did not stop (motor stalled / servo protection / controller not responding). Check the machine on site.</sys:String>
